AI Pharma — Admet_App
======================

This service uses ADMET-AI (https://github.com/swansonk14/admet_ai) by
Kyle Swanson et al., licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE in this
directory).

ADMET-AI is consumed as a third-party Python dependency via pip — its source
code is NOT redistributed here. The MIT license requires only that the above
copyright notice and permission notice be preserved alongside any copy of
the software. Pip-installed packages satisfy this through their own LICENSE
files in site-packages.

The underlying ADMET prediction models (Chemprop graph neural networks,
trained on Therapeutic Data Commons benchmarks) are downloaded by ADMET-AI
on first use and stored under the Python user cache. They carry their own
licenses; consult ADMET-AI documentation for details.

All code under `app/` (FastAPI wrapper, predictor, schemas) is original work
by AI Pharma and is not part of ADMET-AI.

Original ADMET-AI publication:
    Swanson, K. et al. "ADMET-AI: A machine learning ADMET platform for
    evaluation of large-scale chemical libraries" Bioinformatics, 2024.
    https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btae416
